{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And they said one to another: 'Man hu' — because they did not know what it was. And Dunash too interpreted it so, and the end of the verse proves it." "כי לא ידעו מה הוא — And I say: 'Man hu.' And its Targum: של מה. And since it is in Egyptian language, and in that language they were accustomed to it, so that 'man' = 'mah.' Moshe wrote it in the language that they spoke, to let us know — therefore ויקראו ישראל את שמו מן — because they were astonished and saying:" "מן הוא — like מה הוא. And likewise: יגר שהדותא. And similarly: הפיל פור הוא הגורל — it should have been written only הפיל הגורל, since the Megillah is written in the Holy Tongue; but rather to let us know — על כן קראו לימים האלה פורים על שם הפור. And had it not been written at the outset in the language that they spoke in that kingdom, we would not know why it is called Purim."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {2 "[1] 'man' = 'mah': Rashbam explains the Egyptian word מן ('man') as equivalent to Hebrew מה ('mah'), 'what.' [1–2] Targum phrase של מה in Aramaic means 'what is it.' [2] [בית] supplied before ישראל in [1] is editorial; the base text of [2] reads הפיל פור הוא הגורל without addressing Esther 9:24 explicitly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:49.921070715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}